<blockquote class="uncited"><div>my Hotspot is set for one frequency, 434.12500 MHz. Thats all I di was put that frequency in the Anytone. It's the same Frequency for my OPENGD77 on my Baofeng DM-1701, Retevis RT3-S and my TYT MD-9600 and UV390 Plus. Why would I have to do anything else to "Adjust the Frequncy" to match the Anytone when all I did with the Anytone was put in the Channel "CptDonPiStar Tx 434.1250 RX 434.12500? <br><br>I didn't calibrate anything with the anytone I just entered 434.12500....</div></blockquote>If you have different Tx and Rx freqs and are using a simplex hotspot, then you have the hotspot incorrectly configured.<br><br>Only duplex hotspots have different Tx and Rx frequencies. <br><br>You can force the OpenGD77 to use DMO mode split freq simplex, but this is definitely not the correct configuation for a simplex hotspot.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Aug 10, 2024 4:15 am</p><hr />
